==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|bairro}}, {{m|roa-opt|barrio}}, from {{etyl|ar|pt}} {{m|ar|بري|tr=barrī||savage}}, referring to the outer, surrounding or less civilized or urbanized parts of a city. Compare Spanish ''[[barrio]]''.

